{"path":"utility/hash/operator()","title":"std::hash<Key>::operator()","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span><span class=\"t-dsc-small\">hash&lt;Key&gt;::</span>operator()","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/hash/operator()","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"Specializations of std::hash should define an operator() that:","html":"<p>Specializations of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\">std::hash</a></span> should define an <code>operator()</code> that:\n</p>\n<ul><li> Takes a single argument <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">key</span></code> of type <code>Key</code>.\n</li><li> Returns a value of type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a></span></code> that represents the hash value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">key</span></code>.\n</li><li> For two parameters <code>k1</code> and <code>k2</code> that are equal, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\"><span class=\"kw1132\">std::<span class=\"me2\">hash</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Key<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>k1<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\"><span class=\"kw1132\">std::<span class=\"me2\">hash</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Key<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>k2<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li><li> For two different parameters <code>k1</code> and <code>k2</code> that are not equal, the probability that <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\"><span class=\"kw1132\">std::<span class=\"me2\">hash</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Key<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>k1<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\"><span class=\"kw1132\">std::<span class=\"me2\">hash</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Key<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>k2<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> should be very small, approaching <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>size_t<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> key\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the object to be hashed\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a></span></code> representing the hash value.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>Hash functions should not throw exceptions.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>The following code shows how to specialize the <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\">std::hash</a></span> template for a custom class. The hash function uses <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fowler%E2%80%93Noll%E2%80%93Vo_hash_function\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">Fowler–Noll–Vo</a> hash algorithm.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdint&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;functional&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> Employee\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> name<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw130\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uint64_t</span></span></a> ID<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> std\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">template</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> hash<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Employee<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">public</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw130\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uint64_t</span></span></a> operator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Employee<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> employee<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n             <span class=\"co1\">// computes the hash of an employee using a variant</span>\n             <span class=\"co1\">// of the Fowler-Noll-Vo hash function</span>\n             <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw130\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uint64_t</span></span></a> prime<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu12\">0x100000001B3</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n             <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw130\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uint64_t</span></span></a> result<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu12\">0xcbf29ce484222325</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n             <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw130\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uint64_t</span></span></a> i<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, ie <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> employee.<span class=\"me1\">name</span>.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> i <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> ie<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n                 result <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>result <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> prime<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy3\">^</span> employee.<span class=\"me1\">name</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>i<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n             <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> result <span class=\"sy3\">^</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>employee.<span class=\"me1\">ID</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n         <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    Employee employee<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    employee.<span class=\"me1\">name</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Zaphod Beeblebrox\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    employee.<span class=\"me1\">ID</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">42</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/hash\"><span class=\"kw1132\">std::<span class=\"me2\">hash</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Employee<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> hash_fn<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> hash_fn<span class=\"br0\">(</span>employee<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>12615575401975788567</code></pre> \n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/hash","title":"std::hash"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::hash<Key>::operator()","children":[{"label":"Parameters","note":"key"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A std::size_t representing the hash value."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Hash functions should not throw exceptions."},{"label":"Example","note":"The following code shows how to specialize the std::hash template for a custom class."}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":211,"codeBlockCount":2}
